  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowering urban youths with the skills and knowledge to harness the economic and health dividends of the green transition.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project complements Hivos&apos; ongoing &apos;Urban Futures&apos; programme which is seeks to reduce the negative social and environmental impacts of food production and promote sustainable and inclusive urban food systems and healthier diets.

This project will upskill 50 youth in sustainable urban agriculture and entrepreneurship in Mutare (20) and Bulawayo (30). Emphasis is on intensive, precision-agriculture approaches including greenhouse and hydroponic growing; value-addition of produce; and business management/entrepreneurship. Additionally, workshops for 100 participants including youth and other rightsholders focused on the food and climate policy environment and lobby and advocacy approaches will support effective policy engagement to improve accountability and implementation of relevant climate and environment policies including as they relate to food systems.</narrative>
  </description>
